.. |pin5| replace:: |br| Can be set as RS485_2-(B) 

.. table:: RS232/RS485/CAN Connector
   :align: center
   :width: 100%
   :widths: auto

   +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
   | **RS232 / RS485 / CAN Pin Definition:**                                                                                                       |
   +================+===============================+==============================================================+===============================+
   | **Pin Number** | **Definition**                | **Description**                                              | **ESP32 P4 Pin**              |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 1          | GND                           | System Ground                                                | GND                           |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 2          | RS232_0_RXD                   | RS232 RXD signal                                             | GPIO38                        |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 3          | RS232_0_TXD                   | RS232 TXD signal                                             | GPIO37                        |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 4          | RS232_2_RXD                   | RS232 RXD signal |pin4|                                      | GPIO2                         |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 5          | RS232_2_TXD                   | RS232 TXD signal |pin5|                                      | GPIO3                         |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 6          | RS485_3+                      | RS485 +(A) signal                                            | GPIO4                         |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 7          | RS485_3-                      | RS485 –(B) signal                                            | GPIO5                         |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 8          | NC                            | Not Connected |br| Can be set as Relay Normally Open         |                               |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 9          | CAN0 H                        | CAN H |br| Can be set as Relay COM                           | GPIO22                        |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+
   | Pin 10         | CAN0 L                        | CAN L |br| Can be set as Relay Normally Closed               | GPIO21                        |
   +----------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------+

The relay is driven by GPIO20: high = energized (COM connected to NO), low = released (COM connected to NC).

.. attention::

    #) The RS232_2 can be set as the RS485 signal (1 x RS232 + 2 x RS485 + 1 x CAN). If you need it to work as RS485, please |contact|_ before shipping.
    #) The CAN can be set as the Relay (2 x RS232 + 1 x RS485 + 0 x CAN + 1 x Relay). If you need it to work as Relay, please |contact|_ before shipping.
    #) RS485_3 automatically controls input/output direction. It does not need software control.
    #) The 120 Ω termination resistor for the RS485/CAN is **not mounted** by default.
    #) The relay's maximum switching voltage is 125 VAC or 60 VDC. The maximum switching current is 1 A. Rated load is 0.3A at 125VAC and 1A at 30VDC.
    #) The RS232, RS485, and CAN interfaces can optionally be configured as GPIOs, providing 0, 2, 4, 6, or 8 GPIOs depending on the configuration.

